WEBVTT

00:14.806 --> 00:17.726
Our trinity formation has no blind spots!

00:21.604 --> 00:27.027
We are the Three Sturm und Drang Brothers.

00:29.154 --> 00:31.114
Since their tongues aren't black,

00:31.781 --> 00:32.866
they're not Trigger users.

00:32.949 --> 00:35.243
They're just plain weird.

00:35.326 --> 00:38.204
Somebody, please report this
to the police.

00:41.708 --> 00:44.711
This old man came lunging at me
out of nowhere

00:44.794 --> 00:47.130
and started talking about some bee tamer.

00:52.969 --> 00:54.345
Come, let's keep moving.

00:54.429 --> 00:56.222
Yes, sir.

02:30.024 --> 02:31.818
VIGILANTE
A CRIME PREVENTION ORGANIZATION

02:31.901 --> 02:33.736
THAT OPERATES OUTSIDE OF LEGAL PROCEDURES
A VIGILANTE GROUP

02:33.820 --> 02:35.446
ALSO REFERS TO MEMBERS OF VIGILANTE GROUPS
WHO ENCOURAGE VIGILANTISM

02:41.536 --> 02:42.996
Master.

02:43.663 --> 02:45.081
You've been

02:45.165 --> 02:46.332
weird lately.

02:47.208 --> 02:49.335
Ever since that big incident
the other day,

02:49.419 --> 02:52.964
you've been kind of quiet.

02:53.047 --> 02:56.259
Is it somehow related to the "bee tamer"?

03:06.060 --> 03:08.313
You know, I really don't think

03:08.396 --> 03:10.982
I'm cut out for fistfights and all.

03:11.649 --> 03:14.736
I think it's kind of useless to practice
throwing punches.

03:16.404 --> 03:18.489
You're right.

03:18.573 --> 03:21.451
Then I'll start hitting you one-sidedly…

03:21.534 --> 03:22.994
Whoa. What? Wait.

03:23.077 --> 03:25.455
So, deal with it without hitting me back.

03:35.173 --> 03:37.300
Koichi! Hey, Old Man!

03:37.383 --> 03:40.637
You need to show some restraint!
This guy is as weak as a bug.

03:41.471 --> 03:44.891
But I realized recently

03:44.974 --> 03:48.186
that Master is actually showing
a lot of restraint.

03:48.937 --> 03:51.189
If he hits me with all his strength,

03:51.272 --> 03:53.149
<i>I'd definitely die.</i>

03:53.233 --> 03:54.651
<i>Even when he's dealing</i>

03:54.734 --> 03:57.237
<i>with Villains, he shows restraint</i>
<i>so that he doesn't kill them.</i>

03:58.905 --> 04:03.034
Seems like he uses a little more strength
than necessary, but nothing more.

04:03.117 --> 04:06.329
So, in the end, he's using more strength
than necessary, right?

04:09.040 --> 04:13.044
<i>Hachisuka-kun, you went overboard</i>
<i>with that incident the other day.</i>

04:13.127 --> 04:15.505
<i>Although the methods of how you use</i>

04:15.588 --> 04:19.175
<i>the amount of Trigger you're placed</i>
<i>in charge with is up to your discretion,</i>

04:19.259 --> 04:20.802
<i>those drugs are valuable.</i>

04:20.885 --> 04:23.596
<i>It shouldn't be scattered about</i>
<i>indiscriminately.</i>

04:23.680 --> 04:25.556
Who cares?

04:25.640 --> 04:27.725
You got the data, right?

04:29.185 --> 04:32.146
<i>It's about efficiency.</i>

04:32.230 --> 04:36.693
<i>A human's physical functions are</i>
<i>strongly influenced by their mental state.</i>

04:36.776 --> 04:39.654
<i>It's no different with Quirks.</i>

04:39.737 --> 04:43.741
<i>In order to exhibit</i>
<i>an extraordinary Quirk,</i>

04:43.825 --> 04:46.577
<i>it will most definitely require</i>
<i>a very strong will.</i>

04:46.661 --> 04:47.996
Like a Hero?

04:48.079 --> 04:50.748
<i>As with Villains too.</i>

04:50.832 --> 04:52.709
<i>The individuals we're looking for</i>

04:52.792 --> 04:55.878
<i>are people with explosive energy</i>
<i>trapped inside their hearts</i>

04:55.962 --> 04:59.132
<i>and are willing to pull that trigger</i>
<i>of their own volition.</i>

04:59.215 --> 05:01.259
What a hassle.

05:01.342 --> 05:04.095
First of all, people like that
are usually a hassle to deal with.

05:06.306 --> 05:10.893
So, long story short,
you have been chosen!

05:11.978 --> 05:14.355
You win the Hassle of the Year award!

05:15.148 --> 05:17.108
What are you saying?

05:17.191 --> 05:19.652
Why… all of a sudden…

05:19.736 --> 05:23.364
Oh, you already took something else, huh?

05:23.448 --> 05:25.283
Just as I thought,
you're an exceptional choice.

05:26.075 --> 05:27.994
Don't underestimate me. Damn it.

05:28.786 --> 05:32.999
That's right. Take that pent up hatred
and convert it into power.

05:33.916 --> 05:38.087
Let the people in society have it,

05:38.171 --> 05:40.089
Mister.

05:45.595 --> 05:48.389
Stop messing with me!

05:54.353 --> 05:56.898
Oh, how scary!

05:57.857 --> 06:00.610
-You!
-Give it all you've got.

06:01.402 --> 06:05.698
Fight! Fight against whatever it is
that only you can see.

06:13.331 --> 06:14.832
Just messing with you.

06:21.839 --> 06:23.216
Whoa!

06:23.299 --> 06:25.301
A super crazy thing has appeared.

06:32.683 --> 06:34.185
This is bad. It's really bad!

06:42.318 --> 06:44.362
He's fast!

06:44.445 --> 06:46.572
And he's super ferocious!

06:46.656 --> 06:48.074
Wait, hold on…

06:48.157 --> 06:50.827
Pop, get the citizens away from him!

06:50.910 --> 06:53.830
I'll try to keep him busy
until the Pro Heroes get here.

06:53.913 --> 06:55.331
Got it.

06:55.414 --> 06:56.916
Everyone, hurry up and run!

06:56.999 --> 06:59.919
This is a super dangerous Villain.

07:04.632 --> 07:06.384
Oh no!

07:12.557 --> 07:13.975
Are you all right?

07:14.058 --> 07:15.268
Thank you.

07:15.351 --> 07:18.229
No need to thank me. Just run.

07:25.736 --> 07:28.072
-Master!
-He's not down yet.

07:31.701 --> 07:34.996
What the hell are you doing?

07:39.333 --> 07:41.169
The power amplified inside his body

07:41.252 --> 07:44.046
is being gathered to his fist
the moment he attacks.

07:44.130 --> 07:46.757
It's so dangerous, we can't even
get close to him.

07:46.841 --> 07:48.801
We have to contain him from a distance.

07:48.885 --> 07:51.429
No need for that.

07:53.681 --> 07:55.766
A fist for a fist.

07:55.850 --> 07:59.854
You bastard!

08:08.362 --> 08:10.656
<i>He's going head to head with that?</i>

08:12.283 --> 08:17.163
<i>No, Master is dodging his hits.</i>
<i>But barely, since he's being grazed.</i>

08:17.246 --> 08:19.123
<i>He's accumulating a lot of damage.</i>

08:19.207 --> 08:22.877
<i>On the other hand, the Villain</i>
<i>is accumulating more power.</i>

08:22.960 --> 08:25.129
<i>He will attack again!</i>

08:48.319 --> 08:49.695
Master!

08:49.779 --> 08:55.034
This man
is pretty fast with his regular attacks,

08:55.117 --> 08:58.162
but his decisive blow is too big
of a swing to maintain the speed.

08:58.246 --> 09:01.707
The instant he tried to strike me
with his power-infused fist,

09:01.791 --> 09:06.212
I was able to hit him with
a counterattack on his defenseless body.

09:07.713 --> 09:10.883
But with that said,
he was still really strong.

09:11.676 --> 09:13.219
He was fast,

09:14.262 --> 09:18.057
aggressive, and, above all,
he was physically big.

09:18.140 --> 09:19.600
That itself makes him a big threat.

09:20.893 --> 09:22.728
Just as I expected…

09:22.812 --> 09:25.565
Just as I expected, Villains…

09:28.776 --> 09:30.820
have to be huge, huh!

09:30.903 --> 09:31.988
What?

09:33.698 --> 09:37.159
Lately, I've been up against little ones,
so it hasn't been as refreshing.

09:38.035 --> 09:42.373
I welcome that type of huge,
dangerous villain.

09:42.456 --> 09:46.961
What's more, no one will complain,
even if I nearly kill them.

09:47.044 --> 09:50.631
I'm sure there will be some complaints…

09:50.715 --> 09:51.882
Oops, sorry.

09:52.883 --> 09:54.677
Ouch!

09:54.760 --> 09:59.015
Either way, I'm just glad Master
is back to his usual self.

09:59.098 --> 10:01.934
Why are you happy
when you just got beaten up?

10:02.018 --> 10:04.186
-Are you an idiot?
-Ouch.

10:05.938 --> 10:08.816
I thought the person I picked this time
was pretty good,

10:08.899 --> 10:11.944
but those people got in the way again.

10:12.028 --> 10:16.157
Especially that old man. I think
something needs to be done with him.

10:16.240 --> 10:17.658
Not that I care.

10:17.742 --> 10:22.705
<i>The existence of Vigilantes like them</i>
<i>are useful to us.</i>

10:22.788 --> 10:26.500
<i>I can gather data without involving</i>
<i>the Heroes or the police.</i>

10:26.584 --> 10:28.127
<i>We need to keep things the way they are.</i>

10:30.338 --> 10:34.133
But it seems like they're trying
to get something on us.

10:34.216 --> 10:37.219
<i>Gather data without giving away data.</i>

10:37.303 --> 10:40.681
<i>Hachisuka-kun, this is your moment</i>
<i>to show off your skills as a coordinator.</i>

10:40.765 --> 10:44.185
Is that really my responsibility?

10:45.895 --> 10:47.021
Um…

10:48.147 --> 10:49.857
Are you Honey-chan?

10:49.940 --> 10:52.902
Mister, you're well built.

10:52.985 --> 10:54.362
Wow,

10:54.445 --> 10:56.864
I didn't think you'd be this cute either.

10:58.282 --> 11:00.993
Enough with the introductions.
Let's get going.

11:01.702 --> 11:03.204
You're quite impatient, huh?

11:03.287 --> 11:04.372
You sure about this?

11:05.623 --> 11:08.584
I want to see your wild side, Mister.

11:09.585 --> 11:11.170
Just messing with you.

11:16.967 --> 11:19.095
<i>PIT01 to Control Room.</i>

11:19.178 --> 11:21.972
<i>We have eyes on a Villain</i>
<i>running recklessly.</i>

11:24.809 --> 11:26.477
<i>Control Room to PIT01.</i>

11:26.560 --> 11:29.271
<i>No civilian vehicles spotted</i>
<i>within a five km radius.</i>

11:29.355 --> 11:32.483
<i>Roger. Ingenium, into action.</i>

11:32.566 --> 11:35.444
<i>Ingenium, launching</i>
<i>the Hot Start sequence.</i>

11:35.528 --> 11:37.822
<i>Checking function of the cowl suit.</i>

11:37.905 --> 11:42.243
<i>Communication device, no abnormalities.</i>
<i>Alignment, no abnormalities.</i>

11:45.496 --> 11:49.792
<i>Catapult, all set. PIT01, decelerating.</i>
<i>Maintaining speed of 80 km/hr.</i>

11:53.963 --> 11:54.964
<i>Ingenium</i>

11:55.047 --> 11:57.133
<i>Pit Out.</i>

12:12.523 --> 12:16.819
Hey, you reckless runner.
This chase has come to an end.

12:16.902 --> 12:18.863
Slow down this instant.

12:18.946 --> 12:21.449
If not,

12:21.532 --> 12:24.493
I will have to stop you by force.

12:28.038 --> 12:30.166
Not good enough, Turbo Hero.

12:30.833 --> 12:33.085
Put your life on the line when you run.

12:36.922 --> 12:38.966
Later, you sluggish turtle!

12:50.853 --> 12:53.814
<i>Ingenium! Ingenium! Do you copy?</i>

12:55.316 --> 12:57.568
-<i>Ingenium! Ingenium! Do you copy?</i>
-I'm so glad I had on

12:57.651 --> 12:59.320
the airbags.

13:07.870 --> 13:09.997
There aren't many people around
early in the morning,

13:10.080 --> 13:12.416
so I can practice my Slide and Glide
to my heart's content.

13:13.042 --> 13:14.502
<i>There's someone jogging.</i>

13:14.585 --> 13:17.713
<i>Oh well, I'll just pass him.</i>

13:18.589 --> 13:20.382
<i>If I use too much speed,</i>

13:20.466 --> 13:22.718
<i>it makes it hard for me to stop,</i>
<i>so I have to be careful.</i>

13:23.636 --> 13:25.679
I have to work on my issue with braking.

13:25.763 --> 13:27.681
I wonder if there's anything I can do.

13:27.765 --> 13:29.850
What if I add spikes to my gloves?

13:31.435 --> 13:34.355
Whoa!

13:37.816 --> 13:39.276
Careful.

13:40.736 --> 13:43.614
Sorry, I was trying to catch up with you
but ended up scaring you instead.

13:44.532 --> 13:47.284
Are you a student? Are you a local?

13:47.368 --> 13:49.119
Yes, kind of.

13:52.331 --> 13:54.250
I'm Tensei Ida.

13:54.333 --> 13:56.752
Have you heard of Turbo Hero Ingenium?

13:56.835 --> 13:59.213
Of course, he's famous.

13:59.296 --> 14:00.714
Wait, that's you?

14:02.132 --> 14:05.511
Wow, this is amazing!

14:05.594 --> 14:06.929
I'm always cheering you on.

14:07.012 --> 14:09.640
Thank you. By the way,

14:09.723 --> 14:12.017
<i>you slipped and lost control back there,</i>

14:12.101 --> 14:14.603
but how does your Quirk work?

14:14.687 --> 14:16.397
Is something emitting
from your hands and feet?

14:16.480 --> 14:17.481
Well…

14:17.565 --> 14:19.859
I guess it's kind of like

14:19.942 --> 14:21.193
a repellant force.

14:21.277 --> 14:23.195
Can you only move forward?

14:23.279 --> 14:26.657
I can also move backwards
and sideways too.

14:26.740 --> 14:29.910
-I can also spin in place too.
-That's amazing.

14:30.661 --> 14:33.414
You've got yourself a really useful Quirk.

14:33.497 --> 14:35.666
I'm not good at making tight turns.

14:37.251 --> 14:40.254
My younger brother can't even
turn the corners yet.

14:44.633 --> 14:45.467
Tenya!

14:49.013 --> 14:50.222
Are you a robot?

14:52.308 --> 14:55.477
I also lose control
when I increase my speed.

14:55.561 --> 14:57.354
Or more like, I don't have any brakes.

14:57.438 --> 14:58.939
You don't?

14:59.023 --> 15:00.858
I usually stop myself
with the sole of my shoes.

15:01.692 --> 15:04.320
But when there's too much momentum,
I lose control.

15:06.447 --> 15:09.533
Isn't that an issue with the way
you're using your Quirk?

15:09.617 --> 15:11.201
The way I'm using it?

15:11.285 --> 15:13.454
Because you can move backwards, right?

15:13.537 --> 15:14.496
Yeah.

15:15.122 --> 15:18.083
Then, instead of trying to come to a stop,

15:18.167 --> 15:20.210
imagine you're accelerating
in the opposite direction,

15:20.294 --> 15:22.671
so that you can offset the momentum.

15:27.217 --> 15:28.552
I was able to do it!

15:30.638 --> 15:33.807
-The problem I've had for years is solved!
-That's very impressive.

15:34.683 --> 15:37.686
It's still rough around the edges,

15:37.770 --> 15:42.024
but it's a Quirk that can provide speed
and also make tight turns.

15:42.107 --> 15:43.859
But come to think of it,

15:43.943 --> 15:47.363
it's kind of useless, even if I'm able
to increase my speed, huh?

15:47.446 --> 15:49.865
That's not true. Speed is important.

15:50.824 --> 15:54.828
<i>When people are caught in unfortunate</i>
<i>disasters and Villain incidents,</i>

15:54.912 --> 15:56.747
<i>do you know what they're thinking?</i>

15:56.830 --> 15:59.500
I wonder what it is.

15:59.583 --> 16:01.335
Maybe, "Help me"?

16:01.418 --> 16:03.295
Close.

16:03.963 --> 16:06.006
It's, "Help me right away."

16:06.924 --> 16:08.634
<i>In life or death situations,</i>

16:08.717 --> 16:10.427
<i>everyone is filled with anxiety.</i>

16:10.511 --> 16:11.762
<i>It's like being a lost child.</i>

16:12.972 --> 16:16.141
<i>We try to get to them</i>
<i>even one second faster,</i>

16:16.225 --> 16:18.519
<i>so that we can take their hand</i>
<i>and make them feel safe.</i>

16:18.602 --> 16:21.730
The most important thing for a Hero

16:21.814 --> 16:23.482
is the speed in which to do that.

16:23.565 --> 16:25.192
That's what I believe.

16:25.275 --> 16:26.568
I see!

16:26.652 --> 16:31.240
You said you're a student, right?

16:31.323 --> 16:33.117
Once you graduate, why don't you

16:33.200 --> 16:34.785
put your Quirk to use at my agency?

16:37.788 --> 16:40.082
But I don't have a Pro Hero License.

16:40.874 --> 16:43.502
You have a choice of getting
your qualifications

16:43.585 --> 16:45.754
by working on-site as a support member.

16:45.838 --> 16:48.799
You have a special Quirk, so don't you
want to use it to help the world?

16:49.550 --> 16:52.386
<i>We deploy people with the right Quirk</i>
<i>to the right place</i>

16:52.469 --> 16:54.763
<i>and fight as a team</i>
<i>by gathering our powers together.</i>

16:54.847 --> 16:56.015
<i>That's…</i>

16:57.141 --> 16:58.350
REPRESENTATIVE - TURBO HERO
INGENIUM

16:58.434 --> 17:00.936
…the policy of Team Idaten.

17:01.937 --> 17:05.399
Once you make up your mind,
give me a call. Bye.

17:14.450 --> 17:16.452
It's you again,

17:16.535 --> 17:18.954
Ingenium.

17:19.038 --> 17:21.081
Right back at you.

17:22.124 --> 17:25.044
You're running with sharper movements
compared to the other day.

17:25.127 --> 17:26.795
Got rid of some unnecessary load, huh?

17:28.589 --> 17:30.591
You want to remove the airbags?

17:30.674 --> 17:32.634
Ridiculous! That's suicidal!

17:32.718 --> 17:35.512
Your opponent is someone
who will attack while on the move!

17:38.640 --> 17:40.601
Are you finally prepared?

17:40.684 --> 17:41.852
Prepared to die for speed

17:41.935 --> 17:45.731
and to risk your life
by racing against me?

17:45.814 --> 17:47.274
Nope.

17:48.108 --> 17:51.403
I will only entrust my life

17:53.030 --> 17:55.574
to my friends on my team!

17:59.620 --> 18:00.746
And what about you?

18:00.829 --> 18:02.456
Are you fully prepared?

18:07.419 --> 18:08.337
He flew!

18:09.004 --> 18:11.840
So, that's how he's been
disappearing from the road.

18:11.924 --> 18:15.260
He was no road runner, but a bat instead.

18:15.344 --> 18:16.178
Control Room.

18:16.261 --> 18:19.181
Yes. The target Villain
escaped the overpass.

18:19.264 --> 18:21.308
He's heading to Old East Naruhata.

18:21.391 --> 18:23.143
The second team will be waiting
for him there.

18:23.227 --> 18:24.186
<i>Okay, bingo.</i>

18:24.269 --> 18:26.188
<i>Relying on numbers to make a big catch</i>

18:26.271 --> 18:28.190
<i>is what Team Idaten does best.</i>

18:29.483 --> 18:31.360
<i>Catch the Villain in the net!</i>

18:33.654 --> 18:37.991
Did you say net? All of you
are just third-rate wannabes.

18:42.412 --> 18:44.665
Your net is full of holes!

18:46.750 --> 18:49.002
This is the Reconnaissance Team.
We lost sight of the Villain.

19:03.267 --> 19:04.977
He evaded B3 and B4!

19:05.060 --> 19:07.271
<i>Same here with B5!</i>

19:07.938 --> 19:10.023
Don't chase him too far,
and keep surrounding him.

19:10.107 --> 19:11.233
I'll be there right away.

19:12.776 --> 19:14.903
-Watch out!
-I'm sorry.

19:15.696 --> 19:18.740
<i>Damn it. I scouted this area beforehand,</i>

19:18.824 --> 19:20.951
<i>but it's a lot more difficult to run here</i>
<i>than I imagined.</i>

19:21.660 --> 19:22.953
<i>These streets are intricate,</i>

19:23.036 --> 19:25.873
<i>and this Villain can take advantage</i>
<i>of the darkness with his Bat Quirk.</i>

19:25.956 --> 19:28.167
<i>It will be difficult to capture him.</i>

19:28.917 --> 19:30.043
<i>What's that?</i>

19:31.253 --> 19:34.673
Whether it's on the highway,
or on the streets, there is no one

19:34.756 --> 19:37.134
-who can capture me--
-Hey.

19:40.596 --> 19:42.931
Take this.

19:46.018 --> 19:47.644
Wh… What…

19:49.104 --> 19:50.147
Who

19:50.230 --> 19:52.024
did this?

19:52.107 --> 19:53.567
Oh man.

19:55.319 --> 19:57.946
The lack of street lights
and the number of abandoned buildings

19:58.030 --> 20:00.657
makes it very difficult
to capture Villains around here.

20:00.741 --> 20:02.284
But once you get familiar with it,

20:02.367 --> 20:06.079
you can predict the criminal's
escape route and get one step ahead.

20:06.747 --> 20:09.291
You just have to know your way around.

20:11.460 --> 20:12.878
You're…

20:13.879 --> 20:15.005
We are men

20:15.088 --> 20:18.759
who spare no effort to cooperate
with the bearer of justice.

20:20.385 --> 20:23.013
Knucklerduster

20:24.389 --> 20:26.350
and The Crawler!

20:26.433 --> 20:28.810
I have nothing to do with them.

20:30.270 --> 20:32.272
<i>Shall we chase those</i>
<i>suspicious individuals?</i>

20:32.356 --> 20:34.816
No, let's not do that.

20:34.900 --> 20:37.402
We worked hard enough today.

20:46.453 --> 20:47.996
-Whoa!
-Thanks for the other day.

20:48.747 --> 20:49.998
You surprised me.

20:50.082 --> 20:53.460
-You're The Cra--
-What?

20:53.543 --> 20:56.964
What are you talking about? I'm just

20:57.047 --> 20:59.549
a jogger with no special name to myself.

20:59.633 --> 21:00.968
Then, if you ever

21:01.051 --> 21:03.762
run into Crawler, relay a message for me.

21:03.845 --> 21:06.139
Tell him I said, "That was a nice run."

21:08.809 --> 21:11.853
Oh, and about that business card
I gave you the other day…

21:12.771 --> 21:13.730
Please give it back.

21:13.814 --> 21:16.525
What?

21:16.608 --> 21:19.152
Remember how I said we deploy
the right person to the right place?

21:20.237 --> 21:23.365
If you already have a position
you have your heart set on,

21:23.448 --> 21:25.951
I respect that.

21:26.034 --> 21:29.288
Although this is all I can say as a Pro.

21:30.080 --> 21:34.793
Maybe it wasn't appropriate to offer a job
to my jogging buddy to begin with.

21:34.876 --> 21:37.170
Well…

21:37.254 --> 21:38.588
I guess so…

21:38.672 --> 21:41.049
Why are you so disappointed?

21:41.133 --> 21:43.051
I'm sorry.

21:43.135 --> 21:45.220
Come on, cheer up.

21:45.887 --> 21:47.556
-Okay?
-Sure…

21:50.142 --> 21:52.936
All right, let's race to the next corner!

21:53.770 --> 21:55.314
No fair!

23:26.530 --> 23:30.033
<i>This is Pop Step! Next episode</i>
<i>is about how I met Koichi--</i>

23:30.117 --> 23:31.660
<i>Instant Villain has appeared!</i>

23:31.743 --> 23:34.496
<i>Whoa! Someone cool swooped in,</i>
<i>and took down the Villain!</i>

23:35.080 --> 23:36.748
<i>And so, the next episode is "Judgment".</i>

23:37.374 --> 23:40.001
-<i>What? Pop, what were you saying?</i>
-<i>It's nothing.</i>

23:40.085 --> 23:40.961
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
